# Line endings: LF in the repository, LF in every working tree, on every OS.
#
# Without this rule a Windows clone with `core.autocrlf=true` checks files out
# as CRLF, while Prettier writes LF. The two disagree on every line of every
# file, so `npm run format` rewrote all of them and `git status` then reported
# 446 modified files whose only difference from HEAD was invisible characters.
# On 2026-08-06 that buried a four-file change in 445 files of noise.
#
# Declaring it here rather than relying on each developer's git config means the
# rule travels with the repository and cannot be set differently per machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Assets: byte-for-byte, never line-ending conversion, never a text diff.
# A conversion inside a compressed image corrupts it silently.
*.webp binary
*.png binary
*.PNG binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary

# SVG is text and benefits from real diffs, so it is deliberately not listed
# above — it only needs the LF rule every other text file gets.
